   "source": [
    "The `H` in the diagram is the *hash-code*. It is `64`-bits. `V` is the actual value - the thing that we want to store. Because, each item lives in a separate node, different from the primary data-structure - the bucket array `S`, we say it has pointer-stability. No matter, what happens to the internals of the hash-table, the value doesn't move, it lives at the same memory address. This is a property guaranteed by the standard. $\\phi$ denotes `nullptr`; it is used to indicate the end of linked-lists. The green nodes are all in the same bucket chain. \n",
